{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 blind-fixer implementation evidence (held-out validation still pending investigator):\n\n- Primary inference and legacy-explicit `openai:` targets now normalize to `openai-chat:` in `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py`; non-OpenAI qualifiers remain unchanged.\n- Model-class primaries and fallbacks now normalize inferred, configured, and legacy-explicit OpenAI targets to `openai-chat:` in `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, while treating `openai` and `openai-chat` as compatible spellings for conflict detection.\n- `ProviderSession` registers and selects the custom-endpoint builder for `openai-chat` as well as the legacy alias, preserving endpoint injection and the surgical structured-output profile override.\n- User-facing examples in the three scoped LLM/workflow docs now recommend `openai-chat:`. Visible contract assertions were updated for primary, explicit, class, fallback, interface, hosted, missing-extra, and custom-endpoint behavior.\n- Verification: 193 focused visible tests passed across `test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `test_openai_compatible_provider.py`, `test_provider_qualifier.py`, `test_llm_provider_factory.py`, `test_model_classes.py`, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`. The real loopback provider tests remained green and emitted no `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` (one unrelated pydantic-ai event-loop `DeprecationWarning` remains). `make lint` passed, including complexity/doc/workflow gates. `make typecheck` passed: 555 source files, no issues. `git diff --check` passed.\n- Safety: this restores the operator-approved Chat Completions contract, adds no dependency, preserves other providers, and weakens no test. No commit or push was made. I did not inspect, seek, or recreate the removed warning-as-error held-out oracle. Final held-out GREEN, defect-seeded mutation RED, and acceptance disposition remain with the investigator/orchestrator."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787027319915250001,"uuid":"0b88a049-195a-4ea0-938f-a78b86a0e850"}